#
# All static completion data is stored in a single hashtable ($_CDS_COMPLETIONS)
# for O(1) lookup. The ScriptBlock registered with Register-ArgumentCompleter
# follows the same fastest-first strategy as the bash/zsh templates:
#   1. Top-level commands  — when cursor is on the subcommand token.
#   2. Shortcut resolution — single-char alias → canonical command name.
#   3. Flags               — when $wordToComplete starts with '-'.
#   3.5. Option values     — static values for known flags (e.g. --to sqlite).
#   3.6. Comma values      — comma-separable list (e.g. cds add ai,hana).
#   4. Positionals         — static known values per subcommand.
#   4.5. File sentinel     — files only (flags shown only when $wordToComplete starts with '-').
#   5. Dynamic fallback    — calls 'cds completion' for everything else.

